{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies","id":986799,"title":"[2E] Grappling Zombies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-13T09:16:31-07:00","id":986799,"title":"[2E] Grappling Zombies","content":"I prepare Halloween 'mortals vs. zombies' one-shot story for our RPG club. I wanted to use new Tilt Cards, especially <i>Immobilized </i>Tilt to eat victims brains. For this, I need zombies that can really grab characters. What my surprise when I looked on Horde Horror's stats and see that 1 zombie only have 1 in Grappling Dicepool. With roll limited by Defense of target ( at least 2 in mortals, 4-5 in PCs ) my zombies could not grabbed anyone on -1 to -4 dices. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What can be changed in their <b>CoD Rulebook </b>write-ups to make this works? Probably Best At Dicepools but I still try to grasp mechanics of Brief Nightmares. How does contest Strenght + Brawl roll is does when Zombies do not have those Attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-13-2016, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T09:28:35-07:00","id":986803,"title":"","content":"Roll it's relevant dice pool against the other character's Strength + Brawl.<br /> <br /> So if we have a person with Strength + Brawl 7 in total up against a zombie which has Grappling as it's best dice pool, you'll just roll those against each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T11:46:09-07:00","id":986868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies#post986799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prepare Halloween 'mortals vs. zombies' one-shot story for our RPG club. I wanted to use new Tilt Cards, especially <i>Immobilized </i>Tilt to eat victims brains. For this, I need zombies that can really grab characters. What my surprise when I looked on Horde Horror's stats and see that 1 zombie only have 1 in Grappling Dicepool. With roll limited by Defense of target ( at least 2 in mortals, 4-5 in PCs ) my zombies could not grabbed anyone on -1 to -4 dices. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Horde is meant to model Ramero-style slow zombies, the kind you see in The Walking Dead. They're meant to be practically harmless alone, a nuisance at best, but deadly in numbers, hence the 1-die pool at doing anything alone and the 7-dice pool at dragging targets down by weight of numbers. You can think of the stat block as representing a large group of them all acting together. Instead of each individual zombie trying to grapple a different target with their pathetic 1-die pool, they all pile on top of a single target and roll 7 dice to grapple them all together. Since they also have 7 health, you could say each health box is one zombie, and each one you kill reduces their &quot;best at&quot; dice pool by 1.<br /> <br /> If you want more of a Return of the Living Dead style story where each individual zombie is a serious threat on its own, you could try changing their &quot;best at&quot; and &quot;worst at&quot; pools to make the stat block represent a single, powerful zombie instead of a swarm of weak ones. Maybe your zombies are best at grappling and fighting through massive physical damage instead of dragging you down by weight of numbers and being a wall of flesh. Maybe they're worst at discerning live victims from corpses or something instead of acting alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies#post986799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can be changed in their <b>CoD Rulebook </b>write-ups to make this works? Probably Best At Dicepools but I still try to grasp mechanics of Brief Nightmares. How does contest Strenght + Brawl roll is does when Zombies do not have those Attributes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Brief Nightmares don't have Attributes or Skills. They use their &quot;best at&quot;, &quot;worst at&quot;, or &quot;all other actions&quot; dice pools any time a roll is called for. So, if your zombies are best at grappling, they roll 7 dice vs. the target's Strength + Brawl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T11:50:39-07:00","id":986870,"title":"","content":"Return of the Living Dead zombies are the best. You have fast, contagious, cunning threat that even a nuclear detonation can't eliminate. Total body dismemberment just slows them down. Plus, brain-eating. Which is always great.<br /> <br /> Would probably need to shore up on your Crafting rules so you can have a good system for barriers and blockades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:03:28-07:00","id":986875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=986870#post986870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Return of the Living Dead zombies are the best. You have fast, contagious, cunning threat that even a nuclear detonation can't eliminate. Total body dismemberment just slows them down. Plus, brain-eating. Which is always great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, they might honestly be better represented by full Horror stats instead of Brief Nightmare stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:04:59-07:00","id":986878,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'm bit torned now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I started to play <b>Walking Dead</b> video game to get inspirations and wanted to reflect those kind of zombies in my session. But in it, one zombie <i>can</i> easily<b> kill</b> you, just by grappling you.<br /> <br /> In video game first zombie can easily overpower main character and I just get two loading screens cause I let him get me. They are slow, but once one have you, you are <i>dead</i>. Wanting like this feel in play with players.<br /> <br /> And by all means - I look for scenario like 'more of zombies, more <i>dead</i> you are'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-13-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:25:41-07:00","id":986889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=986878#post986878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I'm bit torned now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I started to play <b>Walking Dead</b> video game to get inspirations and wanted to reflect those kind of zombies in my session. But in it, one zombie <i>can</i> easily<b> kill</b> you. In PC game first zombie can easily overpower main character and I just get two loading screens cause I let him get me. They are slow, but once one have you, you are dead. Wanting like this feel in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, part of the reason TWD and other Ramero zombies <i>can</i> be deadly individually is that all it takes is one bite and you're dead. Maybe not immediately, but within a matter of hours. In CofD this is represented by their Toxic \u2022 Dread Power. One zombie shouldn't be <i>too hard</i> to deal with, but you still have to be careful because even that 1-die pool jumps up to 4 if it spends a point of Willpower (which it can do 3 times per scene) and 6 if or also attacks all-out (which as a mindless creature with no sense of self-preservation, it should be doing every turn). When all it takes is one successful bite attack to deliver an incurable illness, you don't want individual zombies having a dice pool any higher than that unless you want your game to be a PC kill fest. I would recommend focusing less on tweaking zombies' stats and more on nailing the mechanics for the disease.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=986878#post986878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And by all means - I look for scenario like 'more of zombies, more <i>dead</i> you are'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well when you've got a small group of them, that grapple dice pool jumps up to 7 to start with and a whopping 12 if they spend Willpower and go all-out. Players are <i>definitely</i> going to want to stay out of melee range until they've whittled the numbers down. I would just put a damage threshold on it - at full health they grapple with their &quot;best at&quot; pool. One they've taken, let's say 3 aggravated, there are few enough left that they use their &quot;all other actions&quot; dice pool to grapple. 3 more agg and they're down to one zombie, which uses its &quot;worst at&quot; pool.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Zombies! Tilt for when you just need that writhing mass of putrid bodies. Too many to fight, just run at full speed or get attacked with a 7-die pool that automatically knocks you down in addition to dealing damage, thereby preventing you from running full speed on your next turn and guaranteeing them another chance to do it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-13-2016, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:26:54-07:00","id":986890,"title":"","content":"I suppose you would need a map of the area. As well as supplies that might be used for crafting barricades, possible 'health kits' that would allow for a little Bashing healing.<br /> <br /> What's the scenario? A full-on zombie apocalypse? Or just a few survivors in the midst of a little breakout, trying to get out? Or are they trying to find the cause?<br /> <br /> If you're comfortable with trying other games, I understand <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_Flesh_Must_Be_Eaten\" target=\"_blank\">All Flesh Must Be Eaten</a> is a stellar zombie one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T00:21:57-07:00","id":987125,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>, thanks for advice - yeah, now I see how <b>CoD</b> corebook zombies can be deadly if used good with all mechanics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to killing Brief Nightmares zombies are - <b>Rules assumes that each one of Nightmare is only one 'Healthbox'</b>? Even if yes, they are put down on 1 Bashing, 1 Lethal or 1 Aggravated damage? Could not find those in corebook. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=986890#post986890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose you would need a map of the area. As well as supplies that might be used for crafting barricades, possible 'health kits' that would allow for a little Bashing healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to point those. Also, could not First Aid kits help to heal even Lethal damage made by zombies?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=986890#post986890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the scenario? A full-on zombie apocalypse? Or just a few survivors in the midst of a little breakout, trying to get out? Or are they trying to find the cause?</div> </div> </div> </div>New England small town had great Halloween night. PCs needed to stay in homes. When they come out, all previous party goeres are undead now. Rather 'zombification' only limited to this particular town, but PCs need to verify it. And I have twist: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> It was started by old Indian curse from uncovering blood treasure by one of towns citizens. Indian Shaman ghost is sustaining plague. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Each PC will have prepared one Aspiration to fulfill - like 'finding person X' for their close ones. Rest of Aspirations are for players to choose. I will use 'Willpower from Aspiration' alternative mechanics.<br /> <br /> 'Wins' this one-shot player that fulfill most his Aspirations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=986890#post986890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're comfortable with trying other games, I understand <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_Flesh_Must_Be_Eaten\" target=\"_blank\">All Flesh Must Be Eaten</a> is a stellar zombie one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to run <b>CoD</b> story to show in RPG club how cool are 2E systems and to finally make use of some less used Tilts and Conditions - and test zombies on those mechanics. But thanks for pointing <b>AFMBE</b> also, even if I know it now for a few years. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-14-2016, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T02:29:34-07:00","id":987161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=987125#post987125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, thanks for advice - yeah, now I see how <b>CoD</b> corebook zombies can be deadly if used good with all mechanics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No problem! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=987125#post987125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAs to killing Brief Nightmares zombies are - <b>Rules assumes that each one of Nightmare is only one 'Healthbox'</b>? Even if yes, they are put down on 1 Bashing, 1 Lethal or 1 Aggravated damage? Could not find those in corebook. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no, it doesn't say that anywhere. The Horde stat block just represents a group of zombies, the actual number of them is highly abstract. My initial suggestion to treat each health box as one zombie was so you'd be more easily able to tell when they switched from being a big enough swarm to use their &quot;best at&quot; dice pool to being one lone zombie using its &quot;worst at pool&quot;. On second thought, using each health box as one zombie is too precise. I would maintain the abstract nature and just say once The Horde has taken a certain amount of damage, it can't use its &quot;best at&quot; pool any more because there aren't enough of them to drag you down by sheer weight of numbers. And then once it's taken a certain amount more damage it's forced to use its &quot;worst at&quot; dice pool because there's only one left and it's acting alone. In my example, I suggested 3 aggravated and 6 aggravated as the thresholds, keeping in mind that targeted attacks to the head will always deal aggravated damage to The Horde due to its Bane but everything else will only deal one bashing due to its Unbreakable Dread Power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=987125#post987125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bGood to point those. Also, could not First Aid kits help to heal even Lethal damage made by zombies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? If you're going for The Walking Dead style, a first aid kit might be able to patch up the wound, but it's not going to cure the disease of you've been bitten. Nothing short of amputating the body part that's been bitten before the disease can spread to the rest of your body can save you. For your game though, it's your call how you want the disease or poison the bite delivers to work (or even if you want the bite to be toxic).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=987125#post987125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNew England small town had great Halloween night. PCs needed to stay in homes. When they come out, all previous party goeres are undead now. Rather 'zombification' only limited to this particular town, but PCs need to verify it. And I have twist: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> It was started by old Indian curse from uncovering blood treasure by one of towns citizens. Indian Shaman ghost is sustaining plague. </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh... Yeah, the whole Indian curse thing is... Not very PC. Your game, your plot, but that's one I would personally avoid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=987125#post987125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bEach PC will have prepared one Aspiration to fulfill - like 'finding person X' for their close ones. Rest of Aspirations are for players to choose. I will use 'Willpower from Aspiration' alternative mechanics.<br /> <br /> 'Wins' this one-shot player that fulfill most his Aspirations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really cool way to make Aspirations relevant for a one-shot! I might use that next time I run a one-shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T02:46:31-07:00","id":987165,"title":"","content":"<b>Charlaquin</b>, maybe then two Healthbox being one zombie? It would mean that on 0 attack successes you will not kill zombie just by missing him woth any weapon.<br /> <br /> I would rather stick to one constant ration on combat scale, to easier count everything. Rules seems to imply that one 'Horde' is like 7 zombies ( bonus 1 for lone, 7 for group, etc. )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=987161#post987161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe? If you're going for The Walking Dead style, a first aid kit might be able to patch up the wound, but it's not going to cure the disease of you've been bitten. Nothing short of amputating the body part that's been bitten before the disease can spread to the rest of your body can save you. For your game though, it's your call how you want the disease or poison the bite delivers to work (or even if you want the bite to be toxic).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm asking here by RAW if first aid kits can heal Lethal? They do not lower them to Bashings?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=987161#post987161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a really cool way to make Aspirations relevant for a one-shot! I might use that next time I run a one-shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Treat yourself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-14-2016, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T03:09:35-07:00","id":987167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=987165#post987165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm asking here by RAW if first aid kits can heal Lethal? They do not lower them to Bashings?</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW a first aid kit is just equipment that allows you to administer medical care in the field, and/or provides a bonus to the roll. Medical care in the field only removes bashing damage. See page 96 for the full details on medical care by RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T05:13:43-07:00","id":987200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=987125#post987125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bGood to point those. Also, could not First Aid kits help to heal even Lethal damage made by zombies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Odds are unless your zombies are wielding or have a special power they will be primarily doing bashing damage. If first aid kits can be used to heal Bashing, along with rest, this gives you a big buffer before Lethal damage starts accumulating, potentially allowing characters to live longer.[/quote]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> New England small town had great Halloween night. PCs needed to stay in homes. When they come out, all previous party goeres are undead now. Rather 'zombification' only limited to this particular town, but PCs need to verify it. And I have twist: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> It was started by old Indian curse from uncovering blood treasure by one of towns citizens. Indian Shaman ghost is sustaining plague. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Each PC will have prepared one Aspiration to fulfill - like 'finding person X' for their close ones. Rest of Aspirations are for players to choose. I will use 'Willpower from Aspiration' alternative mechanics.<br /> <br /> 'Wins' this one-shot player that fulfill most his Aspirations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Ah, nice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wanted to run <b>CoD</b> story to show in RPG club how cool are 2E systems and to finally make use of some less used Tilts and Conditions - and test zombies on those mechanics. But thanks for pointing <b>AFMBE</b> also, even if I know it now for a few years. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>No problem it comes up occasionally. Do tell us how it turns out please, it should be interesting to see this sort of thing in action and how the rules hold up with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-14-2016, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T06:40:42-07:00","id":987228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=987200#post987200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odds are unless your zombies are wielding or have a special power they will be primarily doing bashing damage. If first aid kits can be used to heal Bashing, along with rest, this gives you a big buffer before Lethal damage starts accumulating, potentially allowing characters to live longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, The Horde has Narural Weapons \u2022\u2022. Seems like a strange choice to me, but there you have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T11:47:44-08:00","id":1007355,"title":"","content":"So I hammering rules before Sunday game session and I see I need to make some decisions on Poison/Sickness that zombies spread. Official rules are laconic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD Rulebook, p. 98</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Poison</b><br /> Outside of combat, a character who is the victim of a poison or toxin suffers lethal damage over a period of time equal to the poison\u2019s Toxicity. Some substances deal this damage only once. Others deal this damage once per turn or once per hour until purged, or until the poison has run its course. To resist the damage, make a reflexive Stamina + Resolve \u2013 Toxicity roll. Each success reduces the damage taken by one. This roll must be made every time the poison deals damage, unless the character stops fighting and gives in.</div> </div> </div> </div>In <b>Walking Dead</b> characters bitten turn on after hours, day tops. So it could be Toxicity 1 Poison that damage every hour? In contrast, character dead by the bite turn on almost instantly - so maybe after Stamina - Toxicity turns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-23-2016, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T12:53:31-08:00","id":1007385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=1007355#post1007355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I hammering rules before Sunday game session and I see I need to make some decisions on Poison/Sickness that zombies spread. Official rules are laconic:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In <b>Walking Dead</b> characters bitten turn on after hours, day tops. So it could be Toxicity 1 Poison that damage every hour? In contrast, character dead by the bite turn on almost instantly - so maybe after Stamina - Toxicity turns?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just use the Poisoned Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T02:36:20-08:00","id":1007623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=1007385#post1007385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just use the Poisoned Tilt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using this Tilt outside combat would kill character in less than 1 minute. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD Rulebook, p. 286</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Poisoned</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> This Tilt applies a general sense of being poisoned to a character without worrying about Toxicity during combat. For the purposes of this Tilt, a poison is either \u201cmoderate\u201d or \u201cgrave\u201d \u2014 a moderate poison causes one point of bashing damage per turn of combat, while a grave poison ups that to one point of lethal damage per turn. If the Storyteller cares to continue the effects of the poison outside of combat, he can apply the standard rules for handling poisons and toxins when combat is complete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dealing 1 Bashing per 3 seconds outside combat would kill typical character in 21 turns - circa 1 minute. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T06:42:24-08:00","id":1007689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/986799-2e-grappling-zombies?p=1007623#post1007623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Using this Tilt outside combat would kill character in less than 1 minute. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dealing 1 Bashing per 3 seconds outside combat would kill typical character in 21 turns - circa 1 minute. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, then use the Sick Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T23:18:08-08:00","id":1007959,"title":"","content":"Tilts don't really work outside of combat, they are scaled to work in rounds, which is basically seconds and minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T23:29:36-08:00","id":1007964,"title":"","content":"P214, under 'Poison.'<br /> <br /> 'Outside of combat, a character who is the victim of a poison or toxin suffers lethal damage over a period of time equal to the poison's Toxicity. Some substances deal this damage only once. Others deal this damage once per turn or once per hour until purged - or until the poison has run its course. To resist the damage, make a reflexive Stamina + Resolve - Toxicity roll. Each success reduces the damage taken by 1. This roll must be made every time the poison deals damage unless the character stops fighting and gives in.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T00:01:15-08:00","id":1007972,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> - I have only reservations to this effect that Poisoned Tilt makes damage in number of turns and then, suddenly after combat, it becomes hours. It's... weird.<br /> <br /> Other thing I wonder on this zombie scenario - <b>Should I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007325-2e-ghost-shaman\">Ghost Shaman</a> that cursed city with zombification make any automobiles or electronics not working?</b> Basically, to lock PCs in the town boundaries and they just not 'call the government' or 'jump the jeep and ride in to sunset' before end of plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T00:22:11-08:00","id":1007976,"title":"","content":"It's weird because it's a narrative approach. It's supposed to emulate genres, not reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T00:34:13-08:00","id":1007979,"title":"","content":"It's still weird - like 'you got bitten - oh, I will have some problems by few second, but then I will work for the rest of the day'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T07:34:48-08:00","id":1008079,"title":"","content":"Because combat is a stressful and demanding situation. Once you're out of combat you can take better care of yourself, so the damage isn't as frequent,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T00:35:58-08:00","id":1008847,"title":"","content":"Other zombie related question - Would killing zombie be Integrity Breaking Point for mortal characters? Undead seems partialy like people but then are also inhumanly disfigurent and clearly 'dead', don't they? For now I think that probably first, maybe first few zombie killings - and from there only persons that previous where known to PC, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T01:30:39-08:00","id":1008859,"title":"","content":"Violent encounter with the supernatural is already a breaking point. And, if the zombies turn out to have been people their characters already knew I'd slap another -1 modifier on the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T01:55:41-08:00","id":1008862,"title":"","content":"Violet encounter is still not 'killing' zombies. Should not first zombie kill works on charactet as 'Killing in self-defence'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}